  id: W6_03
  era: A living tradition
  title: Madhubani painting
  text: "Madhubani painting. For generations women in the Mithila region of Bihar painted the walls of their homes with gods, nature and wedding scenes in bold lines and bright colours. After a drought in the 1960s the art moved onto paper and became an important source of income. India has hundreds of such living traditions \u2013 Warli in Maharashtra, Pattachitra in Odisha, Gond in Madhya Pradesh \u2013 each passed from one generation to the next."
